# StateShell Required

Every component that renders asynchronous data (data-fetching) MUST be wrapped in a `<StateShell>`.

## Why
Ensures consistent handling of loading, empty, and error states across the application.

## Examples
// ❌ BAD
{isLoading ? <Loading /> : <List items={data} />}

// ✅ GOOD
<StateShell loading={isLoading} empty={!data.length} error={error}>
  <List items={data} />
</StateShell>
